# Where an object has the scope, every closure in a slot that may hold a mark is one over that scope: whoever calls through the slot leans on it. Here each field has a scope of its own.
# So no closure stays unmade, and the allocation lists no scope: an object without one has every such closure in its slot, and the call reads what that closure captures.
